Board of County Commissioners
Minutes of the Proceedings - Final
Historic Courthouse
310 W 19th Street
Cheyenne, WY  82001
6:00 PM
Commissioners Board Room
Thursday, June 27, 2024
BUDGET HEARING
Roll Call/Call to Order
Chairman Brian Lovett, Vice Chairman Gunnar
Malm, Commissioner Linda Heath,
Commissioner K. N. Buck Holmes,
Commissioner Troy Thompson
Present:
1.
PUBLIC HEARING on proposed amendments to the Laramie County
FY24 budget.
24 - 279
FY24 Year End Budget Amendments
Attachments:
Stanley Walker, Finance, presented the FY24 budget amendments and noted they
were properly advertised. No comments were received. The majority of the
amendments dealt with grants.
Chairman Lovett opened the hearing for PUBLIC COMMENT. Hearing no PUBLIC
COMMENT, Chairman Lovett closed the hearing.
A motion was made by Commissioner Holmes, seconded by
Commissioner Heath, that this agenda item be approved. The motion
carried by the following vote:
Lovett, Malm, Heath, Holmes, Thompson
Aye:
2.
PUBLIC HEARING and consideration of the FY25 annual budget for
Laramie County.
24 - 280
FY25 Budget Presentation
FY25 Appropriation Resolution
Attachments:
County Clerk Debra Lee said WS 16-4-110 requires governing bodies to have a
balanced budget. Lee said this is a flat budget with an increase representing less than
one percent over last year. She noted two revenue sources were down this year:
property and sales taxes. She recognized the work of County Clerk Finance Director
Stanley Walker and his team for the wise stewardship of public funds.
Lee spoke about the fund balance policy adopted last year which helps set goals for
budget reserves and provides a road map on how reserve funds may be spent. She
spoke about the significant future impacts to the county, including data centers,
manufacturing, and an expanded mission at FE Warren Air Force Base, which is
Page 1 of 3
```

### Page 2 of 3

```text
Board of County Commissioners
Minutes of the Proceedings - Final
June 27, 2024
predicted to impact the county significantly. Lee noted that increased growth brings
demand and stresses on county services. She said the challenge with the tax structure
is revenue lags behind services the county is required and expected to provide, and
this is where the budget reserves can help bridge the gaps.
Stanley Walker, Finance, presented the proposed FY25 budget, totaling $292.3
million. Mr. Walker said reserves, totaling around $92.3 million, represented a
decrease of more than $20.7 million.
Chairman Lovett opened the hearing for PUBLIC COMMENT. Hearing no PUBLIC
COMMENT, Chairman Lovett closed the hearing.
The Board expressed its sincere gratitude to Walker and the County Clerk's Finance
Dept for their hard work in preparing the budget. The Board credited the elected
officials, department heads, and county employees for their dedication to finding ways
to save taxpayers' money. The Board noted the county's fiscal responsibility and
acknowledged the hardships taxpayers experienced due to increased inflation.
A motion was made by Vice Chairman Malm, seconded by Commissioner
Holmes, that this agenda item be approved. The motion carried by the
following vote:
Lovett, Malm, Heath, Holmes, Thompson
Aye:
3.
PUBLIC HEARING on the FY25 annual budget for the Laramie County
Library.
24 - 281
FY25 Library Memo & Proposed Budget
FY25 Library Budget Presentation
Attachments:
Laramie County Library System Executive Director Antonia Gaona presented the
FY25 balanced budget for the Laramie County Library Board. Ms. Gaona gave an
overview of the budget approved by the Library Board.
Chairman Lovett opened the hearing for PUBLIC COMMENT. Hearing no PUBLIC
COMMENT, Chairman Lovett closed the hearing.
The budget for the Laramie County Library System was received and
filed.
The meeting adjourned at 6:43 pm.
